# RentVision AI Service (`services/ai`)

This service houses the Python-based AI and document processing capabilities for the RentVision platform.

## Planned Capabilities

- **Data Validation & Parsing**: Strongly-typed schema validation using [Pydantic v2](https://docs.pydantic.dev/) for incoming listing payloads and extraction targets.
- **Lease Document Text Extraction**: High-fidelity PDF layout and text parsing via [PyMuPDF](https://pymupdf.readthedocs.io/) for rental agreements and lease contracts.
- **AI-Powered Assistance**: Planned workflows for automated listing enhancement and lease question answering.

> **Status Notice**: In this initialization phase, only environment configuration, dependency definitions, and package structure are established. Machine learning models, inference endpoints, and external AI API integrations are not yet implemented.

## Directory Structure

```text
services/ai/
├── src/
│   └── rentvision_ai/
│       └── __init__.py
├── pyproject.toml
├── requirements.txt
└── README.md
```

## Local Environment Setup (Windows PowerShell)

### Prerequisites

- Python 3.12 or higher (verified with Python 3.12.13)
- PowerShell (Windows 10/11)

### 1. Create a Python Virtual Environment

From the repository root or inside `services/ai`:

```powershell
# Navigate to the AI service directory
cd services/ai

# Create virtual environment named .venv
python3.12 -m venv .venv
```

*(If `python3.12` is mapped as `python` on your system, use `python -m venv .venv`)*

### 2. Activate the Virtual Environment

```powershell
# Set execution policy if not already permitted for the current session
Set-ExecutionPolicy -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned -Scope Process

# Activate the environment
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

When activated, `(.venv)` will appear in your shell prompt.

### 3. Install Dependencies

```powershell
python -m pip install --upgrade pip
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

To install editable package in development mode:

```powershell
pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

### 4. Verify Configuration

Run basic verification to confirm Pydantic and PyMuPDF import without issue once dependencies are installed:

```powershell
python -c "import pydantic, fitz; print(f'Pydantic: {pydantic.__version__}, PyMuPDF: {fitz.__version__}')"
```

### 5. Deactivate Environment

When done working in this service:

```powershell
deactivate
```
